    "require_edit_to_continue": "true",
    "long_instructions": "#Plan It Out\r\n\r\nPlan your Wrapped program before you write any code. \r\n\r\nWork through Steps 1–4, left to right. \r\n\r\n**Save to your Backpack** when you're done — you'll use this plan in upcoming levels.\r\n\r\n::: details [**Need an idea?**]\r\n\r\nA few ideas to get you started:\r\n\r\n- A hobby or activity — practice time, personal bests, how far you've come\r\n- A habit you're tracking — workouts, reading, screen time, saving money\r\n- Something you follow — a team's season, a show you binged, a game you play\r\n- A responsibility — chores done, hours worked, money earned\r\n- Something silly — naps taken, snacks eaten, times you said a certain word\r\n\r\nPick whatever you actually care about — the topic is yours to invent.\r\n:::\r\n\r\n<br> \r\n\r\n::: details [**Need help with the math?**]\r\n\r\nA few common calculation patterns:\r\n\r\n- Average = total ÷ how many (e.g. total points ÷ games played)\r\n- Percent = part ÷ whole × 100 (e.g. wins ÷ total games × 100)\r\n- Change over time = newest number − starting number (e.g. latest score − first score)\r\n- Rate = amount ÷ time or unit (e.g. pages ÷ days = pages per day)\r\n\r\nYou don't have to use these exactly — just a starting point if you're stuck on what \"meaningful\" math looks like for your topic.\r\n:::",
